v1.0  2026-09-22  OTV4TEST r100 — WHAT THE BROKER'S FEED ACTUALLY CARRIES,
      ASKED OF THE SERVER RATHER THAN REMEMBERED FROM THE VENDOR'S DOCS.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  PROVENANCE — EVERY FIELD BELOW IS THE SERVER'S OWN REPLY
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Nothing here is transcribed from dxFeed documentation. Every event name and
every field list is what `tasty-openapi-dxlink-md-ws.dxfeed.com` returned to
this account on 2026-09-22, captured verbatim from the wire.

🔑 THE MECHANISM, AND IT IS THE POINT OF THIS FILE. DXLink negotiates each
event type before it sends anything. The client opens a channel, then sends:

    FEED_SETUP { channel, acceptDataFormat, acceptEventFields: {Event: [...]} }

...declaring every field it is prepared to receive. The server answers:

    FEED_CONFIG { channel, aggregationPeriod, dataFormat, eventFields: {...} }

...naming the fields it will ACTUALLY deliver. **That reply is the capability
answer.** The tastytrade SDK has always sent the request and always discarded
the reply, so the question "what do we carry?" was guesswork for months.

⚠️ AN EVENT THE SERVER DECLINES RETURNS A FEED_CONFIG WITH **NO** eventFields,
AND NO ERROR FRAME. It is accepted, configured with nothing, and stays silent
forever. Zero ERROR frames were seen across every probe in this file. A silent
subscription is indistinguishable from a working one until you read the schema
— §0.5, in the vendor's own protocol.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  ENTITLEMENT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  GET /api-quote-tokens ->
      level       : api
      dxlink-url  : wss://tasty-openapi-dxlink-md-ws.dxfeed.com/realtime
      issued-at   : 2026-09-22T10:09:43Z
      expires-at  : 2026-09-23T10:09:43Z      (24h; the feed re-tokens daily)

  All events negotiate: aggregationPeriod 0.1s, dataFormat COMPACT.

⚠️ THE TOKEN IS OPAQUE, NOT A JWT. Its middle segment is not base64 UTF-8, so
it carries no readable entitlement claims. `level: api` is the only self-
description the broker offers, and it does not enumerate events. The per-event
table below is therefore the ONLY authoritative capability list we have.

