═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  UNDERLYING — THE ONE THAT IS NOT CARRIED, AND WHAT IT IS NOT
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

🔴 `Underlying` IS NOT THE UNDERLYING PRICE. The underlying price is fully
available and is what the bot trades on: `Quote` and `Trade` on the plain
ticker, measured at 771 and 297 events in a single 150-second RTH window on
2026-09-22. The price is also carried a SECOND time, inside `TheoPrice`, as its
`underlyingPrice` field. Nothing about price is missing from this feed.

The dxFeed `Underlying` event is a separate VIX-methodology ANALYTICS product
computed from the option surface. Its fields, per the SDK model, are:

    volatility          30-day implied vol, VIX methodology
    front_volatility    front-month implied vol
    back_volatility     back-month implied vol
    call_volume         day call volume
    put_volume          day put volume
    option_volume       day option volume
    put_call_ratio      put volume / call volume

WHAT WAS MEASURED, 2026-09-22:
  · 0 events in 45s and 0 in 150s, RTH, while Trade/Quote/Greeks/TheoPrice all
    scaled linearly over the same windows.
  · 0 events across EIGHT symbol forms: QQQ .QQQ ./QQQ QQQ.US SPY .SPY SPX .SPX
  · NO SCHEMA returned in the equity space AND in the option space.
  · ZERO ERROR frames. The server never refuses; it configures nothing.

ALSO DECLINED, ASKED FOR ON THE RAW WIRE (the SDK has no class for either):
  · Series      — the SERIES-level twin of Underlying, carrying the same
                  VIX-style volatility, forwardPrice and putCallRatio.
  · OptionSale  — per-sale with underlyingPrice/volatility/delta attached.
Both returned NO SCHEMA in both symbol spaces. dxFeed groups Greeks, TheoPrice,
Series and Underlying in ONE product (Options Analytics); we are carried the
first two and declined the second two, so the broker's tier cuts THROUGH that
product rather than around it.

🔑 THE SDK IS NOT THE PROBLEM, AND THIS IS THE HYPOTHESIS IT KILLS. The raw
probe built its own FEED_SETUP by hand, with dxFeed's canonical camelCase wire
field names rather than the SDK's model schema, on a channel the SDK does not
own. The server returned NO SCHEMA for Underlying to that frame too. "Our
client sends the wrong subscription shape" is therefore eliminated, not merely
doubted.

🔑 THE SESSION DOES NOT MATTER. Schema negotiation returned byte-identical
results at 15:54 ET (RTH) and after 16:00 ET (closed). Extended-hours access
changes what TRADES, not what the feed is licensed to compute. There is no hour
at which Underlying starts negotiating.

WHAT THAT SUPPORTS, STATED AT ITS ACTUAL STRENGTH:
  ✅ MEASURED — it does not arrive and negotiates no schema: 8 symbol forms,
     both symbol spaces, 45s and 150s windows, SDK subscribe AND hand-built raw
     frames, RTH and after-hours, zero ERROR frames throughout.
  ✅ ELIMINATED — cadence, symbol space, symbol format, subscription shape, and
     the client library. Each was tested and each is dead.
  ⚠️ INFERRED, AND NOT PROVEN — that this is an entitlement boundary at
     `level: api`. Every alternative I can test is eliminated and the vendor
     documentation is consistent with it, but only the broker can CONFIRM it.
     Well-evidenced is NOT PROVEN; this file says "declined", not "impossible",
     and the only thing that closes it is asking TastyTrade directly.
  📄 DOCUMENTED — tastytrade exposes TWO token endpoints. `/api-quote-tokens`
     (ours) is the newer one built for API users, with, in the maintainers'
     words, more limited capabilities as to event types and instruments. The
     older `/quote-streamer-tokens` carries FEWER event-type restrictions.

🔴 DO NOT SWITCH ENDPOINTS TO GET IT. This is the one actionable-looking idea
in this file that must not be acted on. TastyTrade's own statement, quoted in
the SDK's licensing megathread: API users who rely on the
`/quote-streamer-tokens` endpoint will be FLAGGED AND PUT ON DELAYED QUOTES.
Delayed quotes would not disable this bot loudly — it would keep trading, on
stale prices, and every gate in the repo would still read green. Trading three
volatility analytics for that risk is not a trade worth making.

CONSEQUENCE: `front_volatility`, `back_volatility` and `put_call_ratio` are not
obtainable from this vendor stream. Anything wanting a volatility TERM
STRUCTURE must compute it from `Greeks.volatility` across expiries, which we do
carry per contract.

