  WHAT WE SUBSCRIBE TODAY vs WHAT IS AVAILABLE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

`data/candle_feed.py` v4.14:

  PER CONTRACT (line ~1449, chunked 75/frame):   Greeks, Quote
  ON THE TICKER (line ~1729):   Trade, TimeAndSale, Summary, Underlying, Quote
  Candle arrives on its own subscription.

  🔴 Underlying IS SUBSCRIBED AND CANNOT EVER DELIVER. It sits in the ticker
     block, the server returns no schema for it, and `underlying_series` has
     been empty since the stream was added 2026-08-22. The subscribe logs
     "subscribed QQQ Underlying" every connection, which is why this looked
     healthy for a month.

  🔴 TheoPrice IS CARRIED, DELIVERS 12 FIELDS, AND IS SUBSCRIBED NOWHERE.
     r116 moved it to the per-contract block where it belongs; r118 REVERTED
     that on 2026-08-25 after SPX lost its ENTIRE per-contract subscription at
     13:27 UTC — greeks, quotes, marks and theo frozen at the same instant —
     and could not evaluate a strategy through the ORB window. QQQ, identical
     code and a narrower chain, was unaffected. The writer `_on_theo` and the
     `theo_series` table both remain; only the subscribe was withdrawn.

  ⚠️ THE r118 HAZARD IS WIDTH, NOT ENTITLEMENT, AND IT IS STILL UNMEASURED.
     SPX is ~500 contracts (7 chunks) against QQQ's ~372 (5). Adding a third
     event type per chunk was the only change. The per-chunk try/except did NOT
     contain it. Re-adding TheoPrice must therefore establish the width limit
     first — smaller chunks, or a separate streamer channel — and must not be
     tried on SPX during a session.

  NEVER SUBSCRIBED, FULLY CARRIED, AVAILABLE FOR THE ASKING:
     · Profile (19 fields, both spaces) — halt state, limit-up/limit-down
       bands, shares, beta, ex-dividend. `tradingStatus` / `haltStartTime` are
       a live halt detector we do not currently have.
     · Summary on OPTIONS (13 fields) — per-contract openInterest and prior-day
       close, which today we source elsewhere.
     · Candle on OPTIONS (17 fields) — per-contract OHLC with impVolatility
       and openInterest folded in.

═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  HOW TO REGENERATE
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

The capture is a read-only handshake: it opens its own streamer, subscribes
each event type to a symbol, records the FEED_CONFIG replies and exits. It
writes no table, touches no service, holds no lock, and needs no live tape —
schema negotiation happens with the market closed.

⚠️ THE GENERATOR IS NOT YET IN THE REPO. This file was produced from a scratch
probe on 2026-09-22. Until a `tools/feed_capabilities.py` lands, treat the
table as a dated snapshot: the entitlement can change at the vendor's end and
nothing here will notice.

⚠️ PROBE, DO NOT EDIT THE LIVE SUBSCRIPTION TO FIND OUT. r118 is the precedent:
one added event type cost SPX its entire per-contract feed mid-session.
